# Keep the build context small and keep private data out of the image.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` sent a 3.4 GB context and baked two things into
# the image that must never be in a distributable artifact:
#   - apps/server/data/  the live SQLite database and vault copy (real notes)
#   - node_modules/      macOS-native binaries, wrong for a Linux image and able
#                        to shadow the correct install
# Most of the remaining bulk is the Rust target/ dir from the Tauri build.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
static_dist

# The desktop app is not part of the server image, and its Rust build artefacts
# are by far the largest thing in the repo.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen

# Private: the database, the vault, exports, and anything holding secrets — at
# any depth. A pattern without **/ matches only at the context root, so `*.db`
# never caught data/basalt.db. ./data is where docker-compose keeps the vault
# and the database; without it here, a rebuild after the first `compose up`
# copied both into the image (audit REG-010).
data
**/data
**/data-dev
**/exports
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/.env
**/.env.*

.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
